meta {
  name: Add Scope to Entry
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/parlance.v1.ScopeService/AddScopeToEntry
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "entryId": "{{entryId}}",
    "scopeId": "{{scopeId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  # Add Scope to Entry

  Associates a scope with a translation entry.

  ## Request
  - `entryId` (required): The UUID of the entry
  - `scopeId` (required): The UUID of the scope to add

  ## Behavior
  - Creates a many-to-many relationship between entry and scope
  - Duplicate associations are handled gracefully (no error if already exists)
  - Both entry and scope must exist

  ## Response
  Returns an empty response on success.

  ## Example Response
  ```json
  {}
  ```

  ## Use Case
  Scopes help organize translations by area of the application.
  An entry like "button.save" might be in both "frontend" and "mobile" scopes.

  ## Errors
  - `INVALID_ARGUMENT`: entry id or scope id is required
  - `NOT_FOUND`: entry or scope not found
  - `INTERNAL`: failed to add scope to entry
}
